# GoldenEye 007 PC Port - @VERSION@

A native PC port of the original Nintendo 64 *GoldenEye 007*, compiled from the
[GoldenEye 007 decompilation](https://github.com/n64decomp/007). No emulator.

The full single-player campaign runs at a steady 60 fps, and 2-4 player
split-screen multiplayer works on every multiplayer map. This is a pre-1.0
release: the known issues are listed at
<https://github.com/jkdansereau/goldeneye-pc-port/blob/main/docs/ROADMAP.md#known-issues>.
Feedback is very welcome.

Project & source: <https://github.com/jkdansereau/goldeneye-pc-port>

This is the **@PLATFORM@** build. The executable is `@EXE@`.

---

## 1. You must supply your own ROM

This package contains **no Nintendo code and no game data**. You need a
*GoldenEye 007* Nintendo 64 ROM that **you legally own**, US (NTSC-U)
version, big-endian `.z64`:

| Region | ROM filename | SHA-1 |
|---|---|---|
| NTSC-U (US) | `ge007.ntsc-final.z64` | `abe01e4aeb033b6c0836819f549c791b26cfde83` |

PAL (EU) and JP ROMs are not supported by this package yet.

To check your file: on Windows, `certutil -hashfile ge007.ntsc-final.z64 SHA1`;
on Linux, `sha1sum ge007.ntsc-final.z64`.

@DEPS@
## 2. Set up (one time)

1. Unpack this folder anywhere (on Windows, not inside the zip).
2. Make a `data` folder next to `@EXE@`.
3. Copy your ROM into it, named exactly: `data/ge007.ntsc-final.z64`

That's all. On first launch the game generates its asset files from the ROM
(`data/pcmodels-ntsc-final/` and `data/pccg-ntsc-final/`); that first run
takes a few extra seconds. No Python, no compiler, nothing to install. If
you replace the ROM later, delete those two folders and they are made again.

## 3. Run

Run `@EXE@` **from this folder**. On Windows, SmartScreen may say "Windows
protected your PC" because the exe is not code-signed: click **More info**,
then **Run anyway**.

> If the game exits right away reporting missing data, run the generator
> yourself from this folder (`prepare-assets/ge007-convert`; on Windows,
> `prepare-assets\ge007-convert.exe`). On success it prints one line per pass
> and ends with `prepare-assets: done.`

## 4. Controls (defaults)

| Action | Keyboard / mouse | Controller |
|---|---|---|
| Move / strafe | `W` `A` `S` `D` | Left stick (or D-pad) |
| Move / turn | Arrow keys | - |
| Aim / look | Mouse | Right stick |
| Fire | Left mouse | Right trigger |
| Aim mode | Right mouse / `LShift` | Left trigger / LB |
| Use / interact | `E` | A |
| Reload | `R` | X |
| Crouch | `LCtrl` | Left or right stick click |
| Cycle owned gadgets | Watch inventory | B |
| Next weapon | Mouse wheel down / `Q` | Y |
| Previous weapon | Mouse wheel up | - |
| Start | `Enter` / `Tab` | Start |
| Options overlay | `F10` | Select |

Everything is rebindable in the options overlay: *Input -> Bindings...* for
keyboard and mouse, *Input -> Controller* for each controller.

**Split-screen:** pick Multiplayer from the main menu. With one controller,
keyboard/mouse is player 1 and the controller is player 2; with two or more
controllers, the controllers take players 1-4.

@DECK@
## 5. Your files

Everything stays inside this folder; nothing is written anywhere else.

| File | What it is |
|---|---|
| `data/ge007.eep` | Your game progress. Copy it somewhere safe (with the game closed) to back it up. |
| `tools/eep_convert.py` | Converts a save from an N64 emulator (1964, Project64, ...) to this port, or back: `python tools/eep_convert.py n64-to-pc my-save.eep data/ge007.eep`. A straight copy of an emulator save is wiped on first launch. Needs Python 3; back up `data/ge007.eep` first. |
| `data/ge007.ini` | Your settings. |
| `data/pcmodels-*/`, `data/pccg-*/`, `data/ge007.shaders` | Generated files. Safe to delete; they are made again. |
| `ge007.crash.log` | Written in the folder you launched from if the game crashes. |

## 6. Updating to a newer version

Unpack the new version into a new folder, then copy your ROM, `ge007.eep`
and `ge007.ini` into its `data` folder. Don't copy the generated
`pcmodels-*` / `pccg-*` folders: the new version makes its own.

## 7. Problems?

- **Black screen or no window:** update your graphics driver (OpenGL 3.0 is
  needed).
- **The game crashes:** open an issue at
  <https://github.com/jkdansereau/goldeneye-pc-port/issues> and attach
  `ge007.crash.log`, the output of `@EXE@ --version`, your OS, your GPU and
  your ROM's SHA-1. **Never attach the ROM itself.**

